it9175 — what is not ours
=========================

1. The firmware image. The IT9175 firmware is vendor firmware extracted from the vendor's own application. It is not
   covered by this project's MIT licence and it is **not distributed here**. Supply your own copy (INSTRUCTIONS.md says
   where the driver looks for it); it is verified for size and SHA-256 before use.

2. vendor/usb — pyusb, BSD-3-Clause. Its licence text is in vendor/usb/LICENSE. It is vendored so that a checkout runs
   without installing anything.

3. libusb (LGPL-2.1) is a system dependency, not part of this tree: the driver loads the platform's libusb at runtime
   (Windows: the WinUSB/libusb driver package; Linux and macOS: the distribution's libusb). Nothing here redistributes
   it.

4. it9175/java — a port of **OpenDTV** (<https://github.com/jpdcs/OpenDTV>), which is MIT licensed:

       Copyright (c) 2026 jpdcs

   The permission notice that applies to that copyright is the MIT text in `LICENSE`, which this project's own files
   use under their own holder. A copy of this tree therefore carries both notices, and the ported files say so in
   their headers.

The `com.pbcnx.tuner` contract and the Android adapters are original to this project.

